After ascending just about every possible combination in Nethack and
Slashem,
and after watching Sporkhack from it's first announcement until now, I
finally got
up the gumption to try out Sporkhack for the first time.

I created a new account on NAO, and started a Human wizard.
That did not last very long.  In less than 900 moves and under 15
minutes of real time, I was dead, killed by a giant bat on DLVL 4.

Undaunted, I fired up another game and played a bit more carefully.
This game lasted about three weeks, 35448 turns and ended in
eternal glory.

Looking at the ttyrecs, I see that at turn 700 on dlvl 3, I found an
uncursed
amulet and put it on.  Didn't find out until much later that it was
lifesaving,
although I never needed it, it provided some peace of mind, until I
swapped
it out for the Eye of misspelling.  Identified a bag of holding around
turn 980.

I did the mines, where a co-aligned temple got me Magicbane around
turn 5740.  Things were suddenly looking up.  Around turn 6400 I found
a bones of Rocknar which provided me a robe.  Suddenly higher level
spells were a lot easier.   Later sacrificing got me a +4 staff of
matter,
which suddenly allowed me to successfully cast 'reflection'.  I did a
little
polypiling in minetown, getting some critical spells like 'identify',
and
useful rings like 'teleport control', regeneration, conflict.  I
didn't
overdo it, though.

Sokoban had the amulet of reflection, but by the time I got to the
final room,
it was GONE.  The door had been smashed by a giant, the amulet had
been
grabbed by a green elf, and after I killed the elf a rust monster got
to the square
before I did.  Alas.

I picked up a dagger stack and developed my ranged attack.

Later I had a close call with a black dragon.  I eventually killed and
ate it,
and made BDSM from it's scales before I found out that wizards and
body
armor don't mix - period.

Went on the quest.  The Dark One was tougher than I expected, but
eventually
I killed him and cleared out.

Made it down to Medusa, stoned the bitch, went down to the castle.  An
air elemental started slaughtering me.  I used the Eye to port out of
there,
then I came back via the VotD with a cockatrice corpse.  Killed all
the soldiers that
way, then picked up the wand of wishing(0:3).  Wishes eventually went
for magic markers, Gauntlets of Fortune, and a [HoBrilliance.  Was
able to get my
AC down to -40 after casting protection.  Pretty good for no body
armor.

By this point I had the magic mapping spell, so I mapped my way
through hell until
I found Vlad's tower.  I knew I needed those boots of water walking.
However,
I made a serious mistake by engaging Vlad without asking for advice
first.
For some reason I thought his major power was in a gaze attack, so
I approached him blind.  I also believed he had stoning resistance.
Lifestealer drained seven levels from me before Vlad finally fell to
Magicbane.
It was cursed, so I expect it wouldn't have helped to use a bullwhip.
I also didn't know about blessed full healing restoring some of the
lost levels,
so eventually I reverse-genocided wraiths to get back most of the
levels.  In the
end, no biggie.

I did a little egg-laying before I went after Rodney.  With about 45
cockatrice
eggs in my BoH, I felt I was ready for almost anything that I couldn't
finger.
After I performed the invocation, I tried to levelport back down to
skip the
graveyard, but it brought me down in sight of the stairs so I figured
it had
been nerfed.  Later I found out I should have just kept trying.

After I killed the high priest, I got the bright idea of levelporting
up,
climbing down the stairs, and just waiting for Rodney to fetch the
amulet
for me.  I wasted thousands of turns waiting for him to re-incarnate,
and
then foolishly fingered him before he went to pick up the amulet.  So
I
ended up slogging through the graveyard on the sanctum level three
times.
The trip up through hell was uneventful.  I didn't bother to visit my
quest leader on the way up. The planes were easy, except for astral.

On astral my amazing game was almost turned into a YASSD.  I had been
neglecting
to wear both my "AoLS and my =RoFreeAction, so a thrown potion of
paralysis
nearly did me in.  I dropped from 199HP down to 31, with two angels
pounding on
me, one of them standing on the corpse of Death.  Too many HP to pray,
no time to
swap amulets (I was still wearing the Eye), and breaking the /WoTelep
would revive
Death.  Eventually I figured that if I teleported one of the Angels
away I had
a very good chance of surviving the next turn with enough HP to pray
safely.
Worked like a charm.
Fought my way through to the middle altar (after starting with the
Left - lawful),
which turned out to be Neutral.  Tamed a blue dragon, wished up a
saddle, wielded
the skull of Rocknar, to knock on the Pearly Gates with some style,
and sacrificed my way to immortality.

Details at
http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/s/stupermon2/ttyrec/2010-12-12.16:24:00.ttyrec

With this experience, I feel I can ascend a genocide-less Sporkhack
wizard without
much trouble, as long as I don't keep wishless.

Next up - a monk.  I want to see how much fun those gauntlets of force
can be.


